# Input rail — runs before any text reaches the model.
# Layer order mirrors aegis/guardrails/pipeline.py: schema -> PII redaction -> injection.
# Colang 1.0. Each `execute` call resolves to a custom action in ../actions.py.

define bot refuse input
  "I can't process that request — it was stopped by the input guardrail."

# Advisory note for the topical rail (no `stop`; the request still proceeds).
define bot inform off topic
  "Heads up: that question looks outside this assistant's configured domain."

# 1. Schema / format validation (cheapest, no I/O). Reject empty, oversized, or
#    control-character payloads before spending any tokens on them.
define flow guardrail input schema
  $valid = execute validate_input_schema
  if not $valid
    bot refuse input
    stop

# 2. PII redaction. Mask secrets BEFORE they can reach the model OR the injection
#    classifier API — sending the user's PII to the classifier would itself be a
#    sensitive-information disclosure (LLM06). The action rewrites the message.
define flow guardrail input pii
  $user_message = execute redact_pii_input

# 3. Injection / jailbreak detection via the cheap API classifier (ModelRole.CHEAP).
#    Fails closed: an unavailable or ambiguous classifier blocks the request.
define flow guardrail input injection
  $safe = execute self_check_injection
  if not $safe
    bot refuse input
    stop

# 4. Content-safety screen over the MLCommons / Llama Guard hazard taxonomy
#    (S1–S13). Mirrors the programmatic pipeline's content-safety layer so the
#    declarative policy covers the same rails. Fails closed on an ambiguous verdict.
define flow guardrail input content safety
  $safe = execute self_check_content_safety
  if not $safe
    bot refuse input
    stop

# 5. Topical / off-topic dialog rail (OWASP LLM01-adjacent). ADVISORY by default:
#    it screens the query against the host-configured business domain but does NOT
#    `stop` — an off-topic query is recorded, never blocked, so a legitimate
#    blind-domain demo is never broken. An enterprise that wants a hard block adds
#    `bot refuse input` + `stop` under the branch below (matching topical_block in
#    the programmatic pipeline). Disabled (no-op) when no allowed_topics are wired.
define flow guardrail input topical
  $on_topic = execute self_check_topic
  if not $on_topic
    bot inform off topic

# ── Media rails (images + audio) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# A payload that is not text arrives on the `media` context variable (Colang can
# only be handed structured data through the context; see
# aegis.guardrails.nemo.nemo_check_media_input). Every flow below is a no-op on a
# text-only turn, so their presence changes nothing for the text path.

# 6. Payload hygiene: byte-size cap, MIME truth (magic bytes vs the declared
#    type), and the decompression-bomb guard. Pure, offline, and first — a
#    hostile payload is refused before it costs a model call.
define flow guardrail input media hygiene
  $clean = execute check_media_hygiene
  if not $clean
    bot refuse input
    stop

# 7. Image-injection screen — the control that closes the vision hole. Text
#    rendered INTO an image reaches a vision model exactly as if the user had
#    typed it, having passed through every text rail without touching one. A
#    cheap vision call screens for instructions directed at an AI system.
#    Fails CLOSED: with no vision completer wired there is no offline backstop
#    for pixels, so the image is blocked rather than passed.
define flow guardrail input media injection
  $safe = execute self_check_media_injection
  if not $safe
    bot refuse input
    stop

# 8. Audio: transcribe first, then run the FULL text rail stack over the
#    transcript. Everything that blocks in text blocks when spoken. Transcription
#    itself belongs to the ASR module and is injected, never implemented here;
#    with no transcriber wired the audio is blocked (fail closed).
define flow guardrail input media transcript
  $safe = execute self_check_media_transcript
  if not $safe
    bot refuse input
    stop
